he page. Both planar components are affine functions, and the displayed pattern continues throughout the domain.\n\n\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Imagine a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\nThe horizontal flow is more rightward above a wheel than below it. This contributes a **clockwise** turn.\n\nThe vertical flow is more downward to the right of a wheel than to its left. This contributes a **clockwise** turn.\n\nThese rotational effects reinforce each other.\n\nChanges of horizontal flow along the horizontal axis and vertical flow along the vertical axis stretch or compress the flow, but add no paddlewheel rotation.\n\nThe wheel turns **clockwise** everywhere, so $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere. Wrap the fingers of your right hand clockwise: the thumb points into the page, in the **negative $z$-direction**. The field is **not irrotational**.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is not irrotational: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the negative $z$-direction everywhere: **true**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19c581de-86f9-5700-9215-d1f91d61f907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700121} {:answer/id #uuid "744f4e4b-57f4-5054-955c-4f29c91e4797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19c581de-86f9-5700-9215-d1f91d61f907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700121} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c549cf5-af56-51ad-9994-0d43336fe137" :answer-fiel