-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96c56f62-f097-5841-8b9f-6bdd8c8903b4" :question/problem "![Vector field; arrows share one scale.](images/2a/2a67b57192dace6f98c79e76d788cf69678867da4c7bf3c0dd4d6abaa8457e68.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a vector field $\\mathbf F$ on $\\mathbb R^3$. Its $z$-component is zero and it is independent of $z$. View the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis, so positive $z$ points out of the page. Both planar components are affine functions, and the displayed pattern continues throughout the domain.\n\n\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Imagine a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\nThe horizontal flow is unchanged between the upper and lower sides of a wheel, so it contributes no rotation.\n\nThe vertical flow is unchanged between the right and left sides of a wheel, so it contributes no rotation.\n\nChanges of horizontal flow along the horizontal axis and vertical flow along the vertical axis stretch or compress the flow, but add no paddlewheel rotation.\n\nThe wheel does not spin. Thus $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere, and $\\mathbf F$ is **irrotational**. The zero vector has no direction.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **true**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93f2ff72-3620-559f-a107-fad5caccdb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700146} {:answer/id #uuid "d58ab9cc-3b00-58af-9636-39ae309479b5" :answer/type 