low it. This contributes a **counterclockwise** turn.\n\nThe vertical flow is more upward to the right of a wheel than to its left. This contributes a **counterclockwise** turn.\n\nThese rotational effects reinforce each other.\n\nChanges of horizontal flow along the horizontal axis and vertical flow along the vertical axis stretch or compress the flow, but add no paddlewheel rotation.\n\nThe wheel turns **counterclockwise** everywhere, so $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere. Wrap the fingers of your right hand counterclockwise: the thumb points out of the page, in the **positive $z$-direction**. The field is **not irrotational**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is not irrotational: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction everywhere: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **true**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This reverses the subtraction. Use $Q_x-P_y$." :answer/id #uuid "072f6c90-eefa-5d50-88cf-5a2aba8fb79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700196} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "699db58f-cf0b-5fe1-9b8f-5c0ff126b18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700210} {:answer/feedback "Subtract the cross-partials rather than adding them." :answer/id #uuid "7de0a9d4-44f3-5383-9abc-a5b864e9d25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700213} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $-P_y$; the $Q_x$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "ef3f8e81-ee0e-5f59-8c4b-9eda2f80418f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700225} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $Q_x$; the $P_y$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "f504d82e-1e8d-5e51-b5d5-a088de92642c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "699db58f-cf0b-5fe1-9b8f-5c0ff126b18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700210} :answer-field/id #uuid "24bd45b8-f434-5560-8e54-4c9428557449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a865b3e-8322-5207-a2c4-a3c4a7e15787" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(x^{2} + 6 x + 3 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(y^{2} + y e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(0,-1)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(y^{2} + y e^{x}\\right)\\\\\n&=y e^{x}\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(x^{2} + 6 x + 3 y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=6 y\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(y e^{x}\\right)-\\left(6 y\\right)\\\\\n&=y e^{x} - 6 y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(0,-1)&=\\left(-1\\right)-\\left(-6\\right)\\\\\n&=5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Subtract the cross-partials rather than adding them." :answer/id #uuid "041bfb18-7165-540d-bd3b-2e49b323c234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700195} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "7b290fbf-96ec-5902-81bc-30522a24e4ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700212} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $-P_y$; the $Q_x$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "a666c61d-8cf3-5096-b204-adc01d0ae370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700216} {:answer/feedback "This is the divergence $P_x+Q_y$, not scalar curl." :answer/id #uuid "cac23a17-2166-53db-8513-481e0551d772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700221} {:answer/feedback "The sign of the first cross-partial has been reversed." :answer/id #uuid "f6d2a320-471f-5dac-9400-5c21fff1fdc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "7b290fbf-96ec-5902-81bc-30522a24e4ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700212} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4f947e4-668f-556b-81c5-cb0e1dac9df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "465b357a-2f21-5d50-850b-f3ca33afc9ae" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- x^{2} - x + y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(x - y^{3} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(-1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(x - y^{3} - y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=1\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- x^{2} - x + y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 y\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(1\\right)-\\left(2 y\\right)\\\\\n&=1 - 2 y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(-1,1)&=\\left(1\\right)-\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This keeps only the other cross-partial contribution." :answer/id #uuid "0c05033b-2343-5b30-b54c-87b1d1261832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700200} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "18b6b4ed-a95e-5e5b-81c4-ab74b043ec79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700204} {:answer/feedback "A factor from the partial differentiation has been omitted." :answer/id #uuid "53bb9e8e-ffe5-500c-b703-46e2f0a7650d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700209} {:answer/feedback "This reverses the subtraction. Use $Q_x-P_y$." :answer/id #uuid "74f2bbdc-34b1-5c1a-81fb-d15d15d03619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700211} {:answer/feedback "A derivative factor is omitted and the subtraction sign is reversed." :answer/id #uuid "d6575147-6c24-5693-96c9-285969ecef92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "18b6b4ed-a95e-5e5b-81c4-ab74b043ec79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700204} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a5ba692-1faa-505a-963c-f03e625a1564" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "495c65df-f1fd-5cc8-a55f-7e2b4f2f3d01" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- x^{2} - x - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(- y^{2} + y \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 1 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(-2,1)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- y^{2} + y \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 1 \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 x y}{x^{2} + 1}\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- x^{2} - x - y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 y\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(\\frac{2 x y}{x^{2} + 1}\\right)-\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 x y}{x^{2} + 1} + 2 y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(-2,1)&=\\left(- \\frac{4}{5}\\right)-\\left(-2\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{6}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Subtract the cross-partials rather than adding them." :answer/id #uuid "0c9792b2-dda7-5356-ad4b-ee003cf76f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700201} {:answer/feedback "This reverses the subtraction. Use $Q_x-P_y$." :answer/id #uuid "2751cef5-1b86-55b5-9b52-e4fd240f371c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700206} {:answer/feedback "This uses $Q_y-P_x$, with the differentiation variables interchanged." :answer/id #uuid "9d509e31-c5a9-516e-b60a-78092da9e99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700214} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $Q_x$; the $P_y$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "c08e32f8-b57b-5fb8-be0e-663790fef749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700219} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "d80c4d65-fcf6-50d6-8f9b-3fe1521d3067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "d80c4d65-fcf6-50d6-8f9b-3fe1521d3067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700224} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7b8dff-f547-5a57-a7d4-288bcd28b466" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bda0cb5e-5897-5e3b-92ef-3505267c1fea" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- 4 x^{2} - 3 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(- y^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- y^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)}\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- 4 x^{2} - 3 y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 6 y\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)-\\left(- 6 y\\right)\\\\\n&=y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + 6 y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})&=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)-\\left(- 3 \\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{7 \\pi}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The sign of the first cross-partial has been reversed." :answer/id #uuid "109eb2b7-de8a-502a-994c-4383244f2fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700202} {:answer/feedback "Subtract the cross-partials rather than adding them." :answer/id #uuid "15fdcc4c-7c15-5715-9db2-4680b05b2c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700203} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $-P_y$; the $Q_x$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "9ee3c439-0db1-5d31-8226-9810a81050df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700215} {:answer/feedback "This is the divergence $P_x+Q_y$, not scalar curl." :answer/id #uuid "c774962e-2fb9-53e4-a52a-ce05b1a3a6a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700220} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "f2f0dd72-dce9-50ab-ae93-cc6a143c967e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "f2f0dd72-dce9-50ab-ae93-cc6a143c967e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700226} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bcfd9c2-e459-5b38-8e6c-13e0ac74c87f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f87f6483-9b83-53cd-b96c-e7b791dc63ea" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- x^{2} - 3 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(3 x y + 2 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, defined where $x+y>0$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(0,\\frac{1}{2})$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(3 x y + 2 y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=3 y\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- x^{2} - 3 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{3}{x + y}\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(3 y\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{3}{x + y}\\right)\\\\\n&=3 y + \\frac{3}{x + y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(0,\\frac{1}{2})&=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)-\\left(-6\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{15}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295e216d-1767-5d93-bd49-000a8278b724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "295e216d-1767-5d93-bd49-000a8278b724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700417} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a09ff01-ec22-54ea-ac09-afb7ae64a096" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43eaa0f0-dd22-52cc-86d8-711bdc4f8acc" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=1$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, find the general expression for $F(x)$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant of integration.\n\n$F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}" :question/worked-solution "We need a function whose derivative is $1$. Since integration reverses differentiation,\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nThe constant integrand is the power $x^0$, so the power rule applies with $n=0$:\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\int x^0\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{x^{0+1}}{0+1}+C=x+C.\n$$\n\nCheck:\n\n$$\nF'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x+C)=1+0=1=f(x).\n$$\n\nEvery constant $C$ gives the same derivative, so $x$ alone is only one antiderivative; $x+C$ describes the general family."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b33f7f-0ed6-5010-a114-08b13a89a73e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^9}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700416} {:answer/id #uuid "2b132236-db31-5a86-a1eb-52558ac5948e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{10}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700418} {:answer/id #uuid "5092b2af-d9c6-5eb2-8d0b-6cf1c04c348c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{10}}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700423} {:answer/id #uuid "96f982ab-aaa2-5ffd-a137-04d46d1f4b2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x^8+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700426} {:answer/id #uuid "d2953e38-8285-5d5c-8687-9709a1494c6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5092b2af-d9c6-5eb2-8d0b-6cf1c04c348c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{10}}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700423} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a6b5d3-e621-534e-b053-c0bc1433c040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb0a26ec-3743-56c1-a25f-60164f32d428" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\int x^9\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nSelect the general antiderivative, including the arbitrary constant of integration." :question/worked-solution "The power rule for integration increases the exponent by one and divides by that new exponent. With $n=9$,\n\n$$\n\\int x^9\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{x^{9+1}}{9+1}+C=\\frac{x^{10}}{10}+C.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{10}}{10}+C\\right)=\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot 10x^9+0=x^9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2baa8efb-cc02-563c-8076-3b7e3d71ea5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^5}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2baa8efb-cc02-563c-8076-3b7e3d71ea5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^5}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700419} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c90252f-4f8b-588e-ba82-87453d439d52" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89c0b5be-d1a0-5f61-bf1f-567661a4f050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5x^4}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89c0b5be-d1a0-5f61-bf1f-567661a4f050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5x^4}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700425} :answer-field/id #uuid "72538860-e2ca-57cf-b8f4-a18487993c28" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff219463-6af7-5653-a485-d339b1b9ac56" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^4$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{x^5}{4}+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Check the proposed expression by differentiating it, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. The derivative of the proposed expression is $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. The correct general expression is $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression first:\n\n$$\nG'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^5}{4}+C\\right)=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 5x^4+0=\\frac{5x^4}{4}.\n$$\n\nThis is not $f(x)=x^4$. The student increased the exponent to $5$ but divided by the old exponent $4$. To undo differentiation, divide by the new exponent:\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\int x^4\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{x^{4+1}}{4+1}+C=\\frac{x^5}{5}+C.\n$$\n\nVerify the correction:\n\n$$\nF'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^5}{5}+C\\right)=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5x^4+0=x^4=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe arbitrary constant remains in the antiderivative and disappears in its derivative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75603fb7-c5a9-51e8-b7f6-00eea29ebb1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75603fb7-c5a9-51e8-b7f6-00eea29ebb1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700572} :answer-field/id #uuid "09708e45-1f26-580d-b4b0-c98a97bb688c" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0e442f2-a271-54e7-8f80-654deff22cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0e442f2-a271-54e7-8f80-654deff22cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700577} :answer-field/id #uuid "b10c2148-d0e7-5410-8595-bb2a18a12058" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1dab34fc-6107-55d3-b10d-c9eb120d2ee4" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{3}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{x^{3}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{3}}{4}+C\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 3x^{2}+0 \\\\ &=\\frac{3 x^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression divides by the new exponent but leaves the exponent unchanged.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=3$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{3+1}}{3+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{4}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{4}}{4}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4x^{3}+0 \\\\ &=x^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32c888bc-5826-5b51-b64b-1bcab5e3b891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{9}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32c888bc-5826-5b51-b64b-1bcab5e3b891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{9}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700564} :answer-field/id #uuid "3821c9fd-f6ea-5058-a5bc-1eb90b6de307" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92eedf2b-e0ea-5fd8-b4ef-405047a3d6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 x^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92eedf2b-e0ea-5fd8-b4ef-405047a3d6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 x^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700575} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3203eb7-d8d2-5995-8e9c-e8e9d807a371" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "496f23dc-fc22-5733-9883-bf9ff6f1dd21" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{8}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=x^{9}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(x^{9}+C\\right) \\\\ &=1\\cdot 9x^{8}+0 \\\\ &=9 x^{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression omits division by the new exponent.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=8$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{8}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{8+1}}{8+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{9}}{9}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{9}}{9}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 9x^{8}+0 \\\\ &=x^{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e0fa51-63ce-5bc6-8479-4772fc2d2e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02e0fa51-63ce-5bc6-8479-4772fc2d2e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700560} :answer-field/id #uuid "18f812af-1a65-5f83-a221-1110e8ba14e3" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9993038-f68a-5c71-9dbf-8fff7041def9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9993038-f68a-5c71-9dbf-8fff7041def9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700580} :answer-field/id #uuid "72da51d8-78f0-5b09-ae6c-ccd24522f8d2" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54172dfa-98f2-5433-82f3-31dd6dd5e828" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{10}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot 11x^{10}+0 \\\\ &=x^{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression does differentiate to the given function.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=10$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{10}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{10+1}}{10+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot 11x^{10}+0 \\\\ &=x^{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4efd4867-5512-5b91-971d-60b0f9a00d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 x^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4efd4867-5512-5b91-971d-60b0f9a00d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 x^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700568} :answer-field/id #uuid "e302afe6-e6bf-5a18-932e-23ba8a1299ff" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "486a75de-fea9-549b-abe3-43a6f3598aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "486a75de-fea9-549b-abe3-43a6f3598aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700566} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94c6270-9467-57e6-a948-c77b0fb8c8eb" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75889302-faba-51c2-87ad-8cc85bbcab9e" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{4}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{x^{5}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{4}+C\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 5x^{4}+0 \\\\ &=\\frac{5 x^{4}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression divides by the old exponent rather than the new exponent.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=4$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{4+1}}{4+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5x^{4}+0 \\\\ &=x^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff19365c-eb62-5c2a-a0f0-f8d9ff0225bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff19365c-eb62-5c2a-a0f0-f8d9ff0225bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700584} :answer-field/id #uuid "5066c5fa-3246-598e-85b5-a3d2b0500d97" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8971dadb-c93f-5d41-9b68-b5f5ede98c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 x^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8971dadb-c93f-5d41-9b68-b5f5ede98c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 x^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700574} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b6540a-ddd4-5e24-a329-d12b853098c4" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed74f25e-aeb7-5e9d-9561-681703c592ec" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{7}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=8 x^{8}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(8 x^{8}+C\\right) \\\\ &=8\\cdot 8x^{7}+0 \\\\ &=64 x^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression multiplies by the new exponent rather than dividing.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=7$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{7+1}}{7+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 8x^{7}+0 \\\\ &=x^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b835722f-5f14-5ef3-a6b0-cda2668e09a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b835722f-5f14-5ef3-a6b0-cda2668e09a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700680} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2ecfad-834c-5427-8545-7a3cd9d56cb3" :answer-field/key "value-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fe3b3ba-b81b-54e4-b85d-92e29cc9a08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fe3b3ba-b81b-54e4-b85d-92e29cc9a08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700673} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1cdaea-d29c