/id #uuid "e78dac80-7f11-59d0-8d3c-874b74df0d4e" :answer-field/key "point-right" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dab3cb7b-c596-520e-ab11-cbd76cb13c35" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=6$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-left}}\n\nPoint with $x=6$: {{point-right}}" :question/worked-solution "Find the corresponding $y$-coordinates.\n\nFor $x=-2$,\n$$\ny=2-\\frac{1}{2}(-2)=2+1=3,\n$$\nso the point is $(-2,3)$.\n\nFor $x=6$,\n$$\ny=2-\\frac{1}{2}(6)=2-3=-1,\n$$\nso the point is $(6,-1)$.\n\nPlot these two distinct points and draw a straight line through them. All five choices pass through $(0,2)$, so the $y$-intercept alone cannot distinguish them. The required graph passes through both $(-2,3)$ and $(6,-1)$.\n\n![](images/a4/a407efda95c6f357462e5dafbcd38683533656a2d84456b1414a31dd1182af30.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51ef2460-1ec2-5aa1-b266-a905475b2e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/69082b0f9d079c7d1afb351f6429ea3fd19ad67e5dc1affa3048c933f77aa858.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700896} {:answer/id #uuid "5392b0ed-1566-5bb8-91aa-a40c39895676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a3eb48ddae6c0a61639a1bf06b963bbe56fb9f04a894bafa72f4960c67df272.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700898} {:answer/id #uuid "8edfe4c1-18d4-5a30-9af8-124b17d3faac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a1a2943aa4cd0f6ea1f153defad1e898d36b4b85c84d1661f1e38d1dbb9f3b7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700917} {:answer/id #uuid "d850d71d-0a5d-5b57-89e0-36d60ba5a52a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3a/3a0efc4ca48160d145be869fe88359b3fb8da49ce48aba474c5633792846ac36.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700929} {:answer/id #uuid "f801eff9-ff25-528d-9f61-5ab18e1bf10e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/046e16e42d9b8e978771af7f6811db8ce84d59635b57b609fcb72c965dbf19f4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8edfe4c1-18d4-5a30-9af8-124b17d3faac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a1a2943aa4cd0f6ea1f153defad1e898d36b4b85c84d1661f1e38d1dbb9f3b7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700917} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e1c924-52f1-50f4-afd6-cef36ce27d5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b07cf9e-c7c1-58f4-ad17-eee864c78a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b07cf9e-c7c1-58f4-ad17-eee864c78a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700905} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea523f5-538b-5a74-aa3a-d860fe09ff02" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf9e292c-e853-58f1-aa7f-3f5ad9e4e54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf9e292c-e853-58f1-aa7f-3f5ad9e4e54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700928} :answer-field/id #uuid "85a58348-9b16-5904-83aa-03294842f8c4" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "057af2cf-343a-51fd-b774-c40488b39066" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=x-2$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-1$ and $x=1$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-1$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=1$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x-2 \\\\  & =(-1)-2 \\\\  & =-1-2 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-1,-3).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x-2 \\\\  & =(1)-2 \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=x-2.$\n\n![](images/f5/f585c9c05b54be95aca55b281422086eaf7c868bb53dc7f1949ebd2a56486ecf.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "560077b5-31fa-5e27-b8c9-b7602b6f89c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "560077b5-31fa-5e27-b8c9-b7602b6f89c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700901} :answer-field/id #uuid "066e83df-ec84-5618-9559-cd803c690a70" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b110af8-8871-55ea-a3a6-413103bb2e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b110af8-8871-55ea-a3a6-413103bb2e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700910} :answer-field/id #uuid "86e1db98-5739-50e5-9894-af1be7b986a5" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d4431b6-e299-5279-9d48-118f6784ef0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/930ab140366898b219de63fd5acb6379891e39108eb4d4ea7a54ae4c2d4d558b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700882} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4fc50e-4ab3-5259-b657-2a9076a503e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8c353c411299420f50fef1bd9bbe6391b16dfe9cdbb61bf655becd41d8431df2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700886} {:answer/id #uuid "672297e5-8855-53ab-be2f-fb617609009b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6c613ac31220b890d69fb2db001c126fb49d04621c3641d0848973db9954069.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700904} {:answer/id #uuid "73cf02ef-e24c-5494-9fe3-6b9dcbc7ff4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd63a41d04a0a3729537220f26466ac69802e90af04a08058c954b3a0ffcaae6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700908} {:answer/id #uuid "827f01c6-ff49-5d0b-850c-f16c9ef1ec79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/091bc1230b8729d0468ad940937d64dd89b04ae25d82615c8225157e1d191d18.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73cf02ef-e24c-5494-9fe3-6b9dcbc7ff4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd63a41d04a0a3729537220f26466ac69802e90af04a08058c954b3a0ffcaae6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700908} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6129653-98a6-5861-807e-220de942f41b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1118846f-1e47-5c0b-b30a-e8bdc673bfe7" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-1+x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-1$ and $x=1$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-1$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=1$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1+x \\\\  & =-1+(-1) \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-1,-2).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1+x \\\\  & =-1+(1) \\\\  & =-1+1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,0).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-1+x.$\n\n![](images/e2/e2b6910a0221e4c851f7af033e51e9e762eb9e704f15ecb4381a452d1b573af5.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 175921