 :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a7553b-a116-518a-a5ff-350f1a6200b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700907} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a969e83-2a42-5839-a3e3-639adb3c5fdd" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b32f0aec-eb38-593b-ac62-62822a969b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b32f0aec-eb38-593b-ac62-62822a969b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700922} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f1a5876-0f41-5039-a088-12eac5c03754" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "16a74586-c145-58b0-bba9-afeeb3cc0534" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2-\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2}(-2) \\\\  & =2+1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,3).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2-\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2}(2) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x.$\n\n![](images/d4/d4ba35ffbdc7e88a510be218444bfcf752b94f3569c646ddb75b832f1edb1686.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226f7cef-1b3c-5d18-a8cb-283a42748d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/94/9418d1cd5d6d49d028440bf1a073c99f75beb6f29078f58708de5e5ae0ee787f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700888} {:answer/id #uuid "4967d9fb-5945-52dc-8f94-9658333fcb45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3a/3a0efc4ca48160d145be869fe88359b3fb8da49ce48aba474c5633792846ac36.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700894} {:answer/id #uuid "55408bc2-d732-5b00-b91e-15f289796fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a3eb48ddae6c0a61639a1bf06b963bbe56fb9f04a894bafa72f4960c67df272.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700899} {:answer/id #uuid "6f6c44a1-0063-53d8-aac9-80ec19dbea5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/69082b0f9d079c7d1afb351f6429ea3fd19ad67e5dc1affa3048c933f77aa858.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700906} {:answer/id #uuid "c1444409-68f5-5adf-95e1-444eb34aa686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a1a2943aa4cd0f6ea1f153defad1e898d36b4b85c84d1661f1e38d1dbb9f3b7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f6c44a1-0063-53d8-aac9-80ec19dbea5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/69082b0f9d079c7d1afb351f6429ea3fd19ad67e5dc1affa3048c933f77aa858.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700906} :answer-field/id #uuid "555959f8-39ab-5ebc-ab6e-97f68d8018e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700900} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d5c92bc-30b2-550e-a6c6-dc5ccd6167eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d5c92bc-30b2-550e-a6c6-dc5ccd6167eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700916} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad39acc8-e535-561a-b5a1-46cfc14c944d" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e30d999-5c6c-5412-a56f-157c5770c6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e30d999-5c6c-5412-a56f-157c5770c6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700883} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbad4d5e-32aa-556c-8ada-f84e08ab5610" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9cb0a683-a2b4-5541-a623-8bec5655e7d5" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-2x-2$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-1$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-1$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-2 \\\\  & =-2(-1)-2 \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-1,0).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-2 \\\\  & =-2(2)-2 \\\\  & =-4-2 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,-6).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-2x-2.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b89e25d6730d1fa3d19af164d8506e8fd115c92515f8f5ea7651f6f5c51b84.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d449af1-b3d2-5352-9a1a-29f23c69d979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d449af1-b3d2-5352-9a1a-29f23c69d979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700902} :answer-field/id #uuid "44aeb3db-a8c3-56ac-b436-02d8930ebe60" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a993dea1-2667-5e27-9dac-8d5725b3f134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a993dea1-2667-5e27-9dac-8d5725b3f134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700920} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aadefca-67