/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0e1988b-ccbc-550c-b1b6-eacfdb312a07" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x-2$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-4$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-4$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-4.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =- \\frac{1}{2}x-2 \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{2}(-4)-2 \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-4,0).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =- \\frac{1}{2}x-2 \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{2}(2)-2 \\\\  & =-1-2 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,-3).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x-2.$\n\n![](images/fd/fda9429962cb359eb8c9e70137378e1e72273b65d7a968361f6dbd060db07c00.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a8c8c18-2471-559f-a114-179e720a06e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a8c8c18-2471-559f-a114-179e720a06e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700952} :answer-field/id #uuid "18ef28a4-c764-535d-81ea-f4e6a3cc619a" :answer-field/key "value-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref