ne x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nEnter the four table values, then select the graph.\n\nFor $x=-3$, enter $y$: {{value-1}}.\n\nFor $x=-1$, enter $y$: {{value-2}}.\n\nFor $x=1$, enter $y$: {{value-3}}.\n\nFor $x=3$, enter $y$: {{value-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-2x-2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=-3$ then $y=-2(-3)-2=4,$\n\n- if $x=-1$ then $y=-2(-1)-2=0,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-2(1)-2=-4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-2(3)-2=-8.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y & 4 & 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/07/076dd57436803bb3d318897e81216dd59bd0c5450108dc73405898ad94da7dce.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-2x-2.$\n\n![](images/fc/fc293f130f98bed98519e0e90132aa1eb59edf36ca3c76d265cb4167318f6ea9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e31dd9c2-71eb-5ce6-a5c2-d91e0601a69d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e31dd9c2-71eb-5ce6-a5c2-d91e0601a69d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701001} :answer-field/id #uuid "20d24644-c342-5d8d-a64d-ff0d53135e25" :answer-field/key "value-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ccc82db-566b-5939-9b41-90e19d196a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1317300a664b26340a54c1f1d7e2496ebd2abfe1700fe347e26721f1667e2e77.png" :db/id #edb/ref 175921867