2264734" :answer-field/key "value-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17bfece2-d988-5979-93ff-cd25f4efa524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17bfece2-d988-5979-93ff-cd25f4efa524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700940} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8fc7bac-3138-5ef4-adcc-30c23e62ddf7" :answer-field/key "value-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d9d294-e460-5252-a328-6cba8891bed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1d9d294-e460-5252-a328-6cba8891bed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700992} :answer-field/id #uuid "f66faa47-470a-51bc-bc12-12abc3a5610e" :answer-field/key "value-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09a17f32-4c48-5ee4-ad16-fe131fb3196c" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-x-5.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nEnter the four table values, then select the graph.\n\nFor $x=-3$, enter $y$: {{value-1}}.\n\nFor $x=-1$, enter $y$: {{value-2}}.\n\nFor $x=1$, enter $y$: {{value-3}}.\n\nFor $x=3$, enter $y$: {{value-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x-5.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=-3$ then $y=-(-3)-5=-2,$\n\n- if $x=-1$ then $y=-(-1)-5=-4,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)-5=-6,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)-5=-8.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y & -2 & -4 & -6 & -8 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c7/c70b1a457d3c0700d6b73040428ff3db18e954429533595cbbf679953d5449b0.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x-5.$\n\n![](images/c4/c42f7a1a9ed9ee8779e145ed550139a3a25590fe3c3ffb042a3feab18b782075.png)"}]}
